[{"sha":"885ba788ff38c8f3521d577077e7eadadee66a80","node_id":"C_kwDOUfqq7doAKDg4NWJhNzg4ZmYzOGM4ZjM1MjFkNTc3MDc3ZTdlYWRhZGVlNjZhODA","commit":{"author":{"name":"HankGrimm","email":"87528983+HankGrimm@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-09-23T13:24:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-09-23T13:24:56Z"},"message":"fix(research): make the Chinese benchmark audit platform-independent (#216)\n\nThe feishu-benchmark CI job runs audit.py and its unittest suite with no\ndependencies, but it cannot run on a platform whose locale encoding is not\nUTF-8, for two independent reasons.\n\n1. read_text()/write_text() without an explicit encoding fall back to the\n   locale encoding, so reading the Chinese data/cases.jsonl raises\n   UnicodeDecodeError on Windows (cp1252).\n\n2. SOURCE.json pins a sha256 of the raw bytes of the frozen dataset and of\n   every archived run, and verify_archive() checks them with read_bytes().\n   With git's default core.autocrlf=true on Windows those files check out as\n   CRLF, so the integrity check fails on a clean clone. All nine archived\n   files hash correctly only with LF, so the archive is pinned to eol=lf.\n\nWriters also get newline='\\n', so a run produced off Linux stays\nbyte-comparable with the committed archive. No logic and no numbers changed.\n\nVerified on Windows 11, Python 3.11, cp1252: both CI steps fail on main and\npass after the change, and audit.py --write-summary now reproduces\nresults/v1/summary.json byte-for-byte.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"edcad3e859465b72f72aeb4b11aa870b25cefcd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/git/trees/edcad3e859465b72f72aeb4b11aa870b25cefcd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/git/commits/885ba788ff38c8f3521d577077e7eadadee66a80","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs9MoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKCAQACgiJPnINMTTp4QVmpevjcRe\nPkJzVErMcM1zF40vmM2qkdzg+uHXIH5XPhP6xYouT4Mv4V9vjwsReXaUv6AFdh4D\nnNk/Gj+1dvvHHyZMmgo46xXlVdWG+mBLtHDO759FdH40cU17dorLiunTx313OFm0\nQxLDQknUybMXeVcR7krQ8fLdD0BaEh+2y7l3yQBPTLCCnr3EBuq+F19rx+s4dkmb\nXmrIh0/umpfEkURNdPCiBoF8Ge3EMo/rQJrYdl/4ei7rQvGbLAYQnpoznYg4SS0g\nd8b8hlHghj7/cskx0bzV0TvoAetymUM66+7w2GFLbGLMoWe6FMGAicun+HksFZkf\nyvxsOYBYNNhpd9Pg4DS3V3GX54iLb7K5fZcGYWHNCKE8CjsWr5+o78XTKIB9rrdM\n8XkoBlg6ZAZlDv9lODUInMeZYv//PaOqjvj4lsmWrbv68dxmC1oQEaz2kTgBRfN3\nF1U+WCfn8AlUolg44pBm+HDPjz2aWLfwUT/ZHClyelpI5WadACYSx5TChAFooQBL\nKbsHB8uixzY5XjFGQXm3BsCmmtksrMxHDMa6zjhXU8pWA9GdsDPiEPWsD68PiIK4\nlC8lGT98wHL/wGpO+urvyp7f9kD40yzAnGCkExFIe21lEQKXfsRTOWgsZPl3zZ3g\n4Min/909+YzXEapbxG7K\n=LQuF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree edcad3e859465b72f72aeb4b11aa870b25cefcd4\nparent 5647adbc04ffb334652ce8530e3dc26af5c6661e\nauthor HankGrimm <87528983+HankGrimm@users.noreply.github.com> 1790169896 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790169896 +0530\n\nfix(research): make the Chinese benchmark audit platform-independent (#216)\n\nThe feishu-benchmark CI job runs audit.py and its unittest suite with no\ndependencies, but it cannot run on a platform whose locale encoding is not\nUTF-8, for two independent reasons.\n\n1. read_text()/write_text() without an explicit encoding fall back to the\n   locale encoding, so reading the Chinese data/cases.jsonl raises\n   UnicodeDecodeError on Windows (cp1252).\n\n2. SOURCE.json pins a sha256 of the raw bytes of the frozen dataset and of\n   every archived run, and verify_archive() checks them with read_bytes().\n   With git's default core.autocrlf=true on Windows those files check out as\n   CRLF, so the integrity check fails on a clean clone. All nine archived\n   files hash correctly only with LF, so the archive is pinned to eol=lf.\n\nWriters also get newline='\\n', so a run produced off Linux stays\nbyte-comparable with the committed archive. No logic and no numbers changed.\n\nVerified on Windows 11, Python 3.11, cp1252: both CI steps fail on main and\npass after the change, and audit.py --write-summary now reproduces\nresults/v1/summary.json byte-for-byte.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>","verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:24:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/commits/885ba788ff38c8f3521d577077e7eadadee66a80","html_url":"https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya/commit/885ba788ff38c8f3521d577077e7eadadee66a80","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/commits/885ba788ff38c8f3521d577077e7eadadee66a80/comments","author":{"login":"HankGrimm","id":87528983,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTI4OTgz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87528983?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm","html_url":"https://github.com/HankGrimm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HankGrimm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gist